  "chosenReason": "owner 2026-09-26: other-realm veil removed at every zoom. Seeker code 31b, Crownlands at the FAR chart (band 0, d 22, the D-177 landing overview): \"check crownland also have that grey area on the edges, which sunscar had, fix it for all realms, sunscar does not have it anymore while zoomed in but when you zoom out a bit you will see it again on this range\". globe-realms-veil 02e9da84 = the previous pin c41c34a9 (which removed the MAP veil) plus one commit that removes every remaining per-deed other-realm veil: chart.glsl.js (the FAR chart x0.85, and so the chart-to-MAP crossfade; its uDeeds declaration and fetch went too), minimap.glsl.js (x0.12 toward the sea; its uDeeds declaration and fetch went too) and the map.js STUB_FS stand-in (x0.8; its deeds read stays for the deed lines). mapground.glsl.js changes only a comment. groundcost.js: chart pass 5 -> 4 fetches (CHART_FS main 3 -> 2). An other-realm deed now draws exactly as a cell with no deed, as the realm art paints it; the soft GA2-04 foreign fade (distance from this realm deeds) and coasts are unchanged. Stages that moved: rm-chart, minimap, stub-ground, and the three rm-map fragment stages (comment only). The same commit changes realmmap.js (legacy ?rm1, not exported), ground.test.mjs and DECISIONS.md, all outside the export. Pack pm1-cb8faa56909faa31 unchanged (pack-manifest.json byte-identical to c41c34a9). globe-realms carries the same change as 8acdf059 (cherry-pick onto fd338c5a); the side-branch commit is pinned so nothing else in the engine moves.",
